.TH CF-D1 1 "September 2026" "cf-cli v1.1.2" "Cloudflare CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
cf-d1.1 \- Manage D1 SQL databases, execute queries, and import/export dumps
.PP
Manage Cloudflare D1 distributed SQLite-based serverless SQL databases, execute queries, run batch migrations, and import/export SQL dumps.
.PP
.PP
.SH REQUIRED PERMISSIONS
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
Read
\fIScope Level:\fR Account | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBD1:Read\fR
.TP
Write
\fIScope Level:\fR Account | \fIMinimum API Token Permission:\fR \fBD1:Edit\fR
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SH SUBCOMMANDS OVERVIEW
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf d1 list\fR (#cf-d1-list) — List all D1 databases in your account
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf d1 get\fR (#cf-d1-get) — Inspect database metadata, UUID, and table counts
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf d1 create\fR (#cf-d1-create) — Provision a new serverless database
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf d1 delete\fR (#cf-d1-delete) — Delete a database
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf d1 query\fR (#cf-d1-query) — Execute SQL statements (SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf d1 export\fR (#cf-d1-export) — Export database schema and table rows as SQL dump
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcf d1 import\fR (#cf-d1-import) — Execute SQL commands from a \fB.sql\fR file
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf d1 list\fR"
.PP
Lists all D1 databases in your account.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf d1 list [--name <filter>] [--page <num>] [--per-page <num>]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf d1 list
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf d1 create\fR"
.PP
Provisions a new serverless D1 database.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf d1 create --name <database-name> [--location-hint <region>]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf d1 create --name production-db
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf d1 query\fR / \fBcf d1 execute\fR"
.PP
Executes SQL statements directly against your D1 database with parameterized query support.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf d1 query "<sql-statement>" --database <name-or-id> [flags]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBFlags\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
.TP
\fB--database <name-or-id>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fIrequired\fR Database name or UUID
.TP
\fB--sql <statement>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR Alternative to positional SQL argument
.TP
\fB--params <json-array>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR JSON array of bind parameters for prepared statements
.TP
\fB--output <format>\fR
\fIType:\fR string | \fIDescription:\fR \fBjson\fR or \fBcsv\fR; anything else, including \fByaml\fR, falls back to the table. This is currently the only command that acts on \fB--output\fR
.RE
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExamples\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Query table and format as an ASCII table
cf d1 query "SELECT id, email, created_at FROM users LIMIT 10;" --database production-db

# Run parameterized INSERT
cf d1 query "INSERT INTO users (email, role) VALUES (?, ?);" --database production-db --params '["dev@example.com", "admin"]'

# Extract query results directly as JSON
cf d1 query "SELECT * FROM orders WHERE status='pending';" --database production-db --output json | jq '.'
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf d1 export\fR & \fBcf d1 import\fR"
.PP
Perform database backups, migrations, and seed scripts.
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Export full database schema and data to SQL dump file
cf d1 export --database production-db --output-file backup.sql

# Import and execute SQL statements from a file
cf d1 import --database production-db --file schema.sql
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SS "\fBcf d1 delete\fR"
.PP
Destroys a D1 database and all stored data.
.PP
.PP
\fBSyntax\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf d1 delete --database <name-or-id> [--yes]
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
\fBExample\fR
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf d1 delete --database test-db --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
